1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,849
Customer invoicing tracks what your
department bills to its customers.

2
00:00:04,190 --> 00:00:07,809
In our fictional Chicago Fire
practice department, the Invoicing

3
00:00:07,809 --> 00:00:12,000
page shows Invoices, Rate Cards,
Aging and Billing settings.

4
00:00:12,310 --> 00:00:15,239
The list is empty, and the
balance tiles show zero.

5
00:00:15,659 --> 00:00:18,860
Read these as the current
account contents, not proof

6
00:00:18,860 --> 00:00:20,139
that payments were collected.

7
00:00:20,559 --> 00:00:23,590
This walkthrough inspects
configuration and account views;

8
00:00:23,889 --> 00:00:28,110
we leave New invoice unused and
keep all financial data unchanged.

9
00:00:28,310 --> 00:00:32,259
Choose Billing settings to inspect
what invoices say about the department.

10
00:00:32,810 --> 00:00:36,389
Billing identity contains Legal
business name and the remit-to

11
00:00:36,389 --> 00:00:40,630
address, with city, state or
province, postal code and country.

12
00:00:41,109 --> 00:00:44,399
These fields supply the identity
used on invoice documents.

13
00:00:44,709 --> 00:00:46,410
They are blank in this exercise.

14
00:00:46,830 --> 00:00:51,020
An empty form may be showing initial
defaults; it is not evidence that a

15
00:00:51,020 --> 00:00:53,260
complete billing identity has been saved.

16
00:00:53,699 --> 00:00:56,330
Identify the needed
organizational information

17
00:00:56,330 --> 00:00:58,489
before planning any later change.

18
00:00:58,599 --> 00:01:04,400
The Registrations section separates tax
registrations, SAM UEI, CAGE code and

19
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:06,540
workers’ compensation account information.

20
00:01:06,950 --> 00:01:08,459
Each field is empty here.

21
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:11,789
These are distinct
organization identifiers, not

22
00:01:11,789 --> 00:01:13,370
interchangeable account names.

23
00:01:13,919 --> 00:01:16,900
Invoice footer supplies
text printed under totals.

24
00:01:17,219 --> 00:01:21,090
Below it, Pay link expiry is
thirty days and the Show a Pay

25
00:01:21,090 --> 00:01:22,990
online link preference is checked.

26
00:01:23,299 --> 00:01:26,799
That display preference alone does
not establish a usable payment

27
00:01:26,799 --> 00:01:28,600
connection or generate a link.

28
00:01:28,959 --> 00:01:31,199
We inspect the controls
without using Save.

29
00:01:31,579 --> 00:01:35,670
Rate Cards describes the charge
schedule: unit or personnel time,

30
00:01:35,770 --> 00:01:38,380
flat fees, mileage and materials.

31
00:01:38,730 --> 00:01:42,270
A customer can pin a card instead
of using the department default.

32
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:45,520
The catalog currently
says No rate cards yet.

33
00:01:46,009 --> 00:01:48,329
New rate card opens the definition form.

34
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:51,849
Name and Description are
blank; Department default is

35
00:01:51,929 --> 00:01:54,040
unchecked and Active is checked.

36
00:01:54,429 --> 00:01:57,909
The items panel says to save
the card before adding items.

37
00:01:58,249 --> 00:02:02,700
This is an unsaved form, with no
charge items or default card created.

38
00:02:02,950 --> 00:02:08,169
For customer-specific settings, open
Contacts and use View on Academy Logistics

39
00:02:08,169 --> 00:02:10,459
Desk, our existing fictional company.

40
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:15,529
Its Billing section says No billing
profile yet and No invoices.

41
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:19,429
A directory contact and a billing
profile are separate records.

42
00:02:19,769 --> 00:02:24,369
Set up billing profile opens a form
for that contact; it does not itself

43
00:02:24,369 --> 00:02:26,699
save a profile or issue an invoice.

44
00:02:27,019 --> 00:02:29,709
Keep that distinction when
assessing whether a customer is

45
00:02:29,769 --> 00:02:31,310
actually ready for invoicing.

46
00:02:31,549 --> 00:02:35,929
The new customer form shows thirty
net days, a blank Default discount,

47
00:02:36,159 --> 00:02:39,860
and department-default choices for
Rate card and Default rate schedule.

48
00:02:40,389 --> 00:02:44,589
Customer terms help set an unset
invoice due date when it moves to Sent;

49
00:02:44,879 --> 00:02:46,839
contract terms can take precedence.

50
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:49,729
The discount is a default for a new draft.

51
00:02:50,159 --> 00:02:53,440
The schedule help concerns
contractor bids and deployments

52
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:55,259
when no contract names a schedule.

53
00:02:55,749 --> 00:02:59,460
Purchase order required is
unchecked and Active is checked.

54
00:02:59,819 --> 00:03:03,819
These are unsaved preferences, not
completed invoice transactions.

55
00:03:04,029 --> 00:03:06,470
Use the contact’s mailing
address is checked.

56
00:03:06,880 --> 00:03:10,409
That selects an address source;
it does not verify that the

57
00:03:10,409 --> 00:03:12,159
directory address is complete.

58
00:03:12,550 --> 00:03:17,130
Tax exempt is unchecked, with a blank
Tax rate and empty component rows for

59
00:03:17,130 --> 00:03:19,449
Name, Rate and Registration number.

60
00:03:19,770 --> 00:03:22,469
The form supports up to
three named components.

61
00:03:22,889 --> 00:03:25,569
Notes, Cancel and Save appear below.

62
00:03:26,010 --> 00:03:29,739
Use only organization-approved
values in a real billing setup.

63
00:03:30,090 --> 00:03:33,209
For this inspection, leave
all fields unchanged and do

64
00:03:33,209 --> 00:03:34,959
not save a customer profile.

65
00:03:35,040 --> 00:03:39,259
Aging groups positive outstanding
balances by how far they are past due.

66
00:03:39,770 --> 00:03:44,130
Read Current, one to thirty,
thirty-one to sixty, sixty-one to

67
00:03:44,130 --> 00:03:48,800
ninety, and ninety-plus days with
Total and the displayed as-of time.

68
00:03:49,329 --> 00:03:53,960
Here every bucket is zero and the
page says No outstanding invoices.

69
00:03:54,320 --> 00:03:56,800
That is consistent with
the empty invoice account.

70
00:03:57,150 --> 00:04:00,109
It does not demonstrate receipt
of a payment, a collection

71
00:04:00,109 --> 00:04:02,169
action or a customer settlement.

72
00:04:02,570 --> 00:04:06,699
Review the underlying invoice before
acting on a populated aging result.

73
00:04:06,799 --> 00:04:10,260
The department menu has a separate
Subscription and Billing entry.

74
00:04:10,730 --> 00:04:13,760
Use that to review the
department’s Resgrid service plan.

75
00:04:14,330 --> 00:04:18,379
Subscription Plan and Billing concerns
the department’s subscription, not

76
00:04:18,379 --> 00:04:20,539
invoices to Academy Logistics Desk.

77
00:04:21,029 --> 00:04:23,679
This department displays
a Legacy Plan notice.

78
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:28,009
Selecting Entities shows Active
Legacy Subscription rather

79
00:04:28,009 --> 00:04:29,629
than an entity-selection form.

80
00:04:30,090 --> 00:04:32,509
Read the notices that apply
to your own department.

81
00:04:33,049 --> 00:04:37,049
The example’s displayed legacy amounts
and counters should not be used to

82
00:04:37,049 --> 00:04:39,610
price another plan or infer its limits.

83
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:43,239
No purchase, cancellation
or payment-detail change

84
00:04:43,270 --> 00:04:44,390
is part of this review.

85
00:04:44,690 --> 00:04:49,100
The final Invoicing view still
shows no invoices, zero outstanding

86
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:51,370
balance and zero overdue balance.

87
00:04:51,770 --> 00:04:56,209
Reviewing an unsaved rate card or
customer form has not created an invoice.

88
00:04:56,719 --> 00:05:00,980
Keep your review notes specific: which
identity fields need confirmation,

89
00:05:01,230 --> 00:05:05,490
which customer defaults need a decision,
and which subscription notice applies.

90
00:05:05,939 --> 00:05:09,789
A form inspected is different
from a configuration saved or

91
00:05:09,789 --> 00:05:11,400
a financial action completed.

92
00:05:11,599 --> 00:05:14,909
Chicago Fire can distinguish a
training-service customer from

93
00:05:14,909 --> 00:05:16,319
its department subscription.

94
00:05:16,790 --> 00:05:20,169
Community care and mental-health
teams can review an operational

95
00:05:20,169 --> 00:05:23,999
partner’s billing setup without
putting client histories into Notes.

96
00:05:24,459 --> 00:05:28,030
Search-and-rescue coordinators can
identify the intended customer for

97
00:05:28,030 --> 00:05:32,300
an exercise; security teams can
separate a customer-specific rate

98
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:33,999
card from the department default.

99
00:05:34,509 --> 00:05:38,989
Wildland teams can review a bounded
customer account, and industrial teams can

100
00:05:38,989 --> 00:05:41,280
inspect outstanding-balance categories.

101
00:05:41,759 --> 00:05:46,460
In all six settings, confirm the
organization, customer and account scope

102
00:05:46,550 --> 00:05:48,969
before any authorized financial change.

